{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "HqFIzbIIzc", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-22", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 908934, "segment_id": "yO0sgOy1w9", "segment_broadcast_id": "HqFIzbIIzc", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Charles Gibson (New York)", "segment_description": null, "segment_duration": 60, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 908934, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "HqFIzbIIzc", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-22", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 908934, "segment_id": "d4z0t5O35F", "segment_broadcast_id": "HqFIzbIIzc", "segment_title": "Economy: Stocks / Jobs", "segment_description": "(Studio: Charles Gibson)  More economic aftershocks sending stocks into another plunge reported.  \n\n(Studio: Betsy Stark)  Evidence of a global recession examined; scenes shown from the market floors; world market and earnings reports from Boeing, Merck and Wachovia statistics cited.  [Johnson Illington Advisors Hugh JOHNSON&#134;- says this is a global problem that is intensifying; notes the next two quarters are expected to be poor for earnings.]  [W.J. Blum and Sons trader Patrick CASEY&#134;- reacts to the company numbers.]  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson)  New Labor Department numbers on mass layoffs in September cited.  \n\n(New York: David Muir)  The impact of job cuts on the American worker in this recession examined; details given about cuts at Merck, Yahoo, PepsiCo and Best Buy.  [Howell, New Jersey, Michael and Roseanne RAYNOR&#134;- talk about their job hunting.]  [Economic Policy Inst. Lawrence MISHEL&#134;- predicts large-scale cutbacks.]  [Women for Hire CEO Tory JOHNSON&#134;- comments on people supplementing their incomes.] ", "segment_duration": 280, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63060.0", "legacy_segment_id": 908935, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "HqFIzbIIzc", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-22", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 908934, "segment_id": "eMNFASVZlY", "segment_broadcast_id": "HqFIzbIIzc", "segment_title": "Campaign 2008 / Obama vs. McCain / Virginia, New Hampshire", "segment_description": "(Studio: Charles Gibson)  Senator Barack Obama's campaign in Virginia while Senator John McCain campaigned in New Hampshire noted.  \n\n(Leesburg, Virginia: Jake Tapper)  Obama's campaign in the state of Virginia featured; details given about his fund-raising advantage.  [In Richmond, OBAMA&nbsp- speaks about national security and McCain; comments on Senator Joe Biden's core point that the next administration will be tested; accuses McCain of fighting for Joe, the hedge fund manager.]  \n\n(New Hampshire: David Wright)  McCain's campaign in New Hampshire, a state where he has had two comebacks, featured.  [McCAIN&nbsp- says \"get out the vote\"; opposes Obama's redistribution of wealth ]  [In September 2007 and now, New Hampshire voter Peter ATEN&#134;- changes his mind about McCain.]  Automated phone call for McCain from former New York City Mayor Rudolph Giuliani stating Obama is soft on crime played.  Findings of a new ABC News/\"Washington Post\" poll on the vice presidential choice {Governor Sarah Palin} cited and how much the Republicans have spent on dressing Palin.  [Republican strategist Todd HARRIS&#134;- says people will criticizes the spending on Palin.]  McCain's coming campaigning in Florida noted.  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson)  Poll findings on Obama's lead over McCain noted.  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson; Washington: George Stephanopoulos)  How Obama's money advantage shows up in the state level high-tech/high-touch campaigns and how early voting is going on in places like Ohio, North Carolina, Iowa and New Mexico and with black voters coming out early discussed. ", "segment_duration": 420, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63340.0", "legacy_segment_id": 908936, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "HqFIzbIIzc", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-22", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 908934, "segment_id": "l9pPQMR45r", "segment_broadcast_id": "HqFIzbIIzc", "segment_title": "Afghanistan War", "segment_description": "(Studio: Charles Gibson)  The deaths of three soldiers in the US-led coalition and of nine Afghan soldiers in an air strike in Afghanistan reported. ", "segment_duration": 20, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63760.0", "legacy_segment_id": 908937, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "HqFIzbIIzc", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-22", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distrib